# Discord watcher extension (`extension/`)

Plain MV3, no bundler, no npm. Content script observes the **open** Discord channel's DOM with a
`MutationObserver` and POSTs one minimal trigger to `http://127.0.0.1:48620` via the service
worker. Nothing else: no Discord API, no bot token, no WebSocket interception, no OCR, no link
opening (hard rule 6/7). Never widen host permissions beyond `discord.com` + the bridge origin.

## Live-verified Discord DOM (2026-09-24, Comet/Chromium) — `content/selectors.js`

`ol[data-list-id="chat-messages"]`, `li#chat-messages-<channel>-<message>`, `#message-content-*`,
`#message-accessories-*` (embeds: title / description), `time[datetime]`, username header with
`data-text` and an `APP` bot tag (strip the badge before name matching). The alert author uses a
**default avatar → no user id in the DOM**: the *Sender user id* option must stay empty for it
(a configured id fails closed, by design). Selector status lives in that file's header comment;
change it only from a live DOM inspection and record the date.

## Matcher parity

`shared/matcher.js` and `src/amore_ocarina_sniper/matching.py` must produce identical results.
Shared vectors: `tests/test_matching.py` (Python) and `tests/test_extension_matcher.py` (runs
the JS in Node/Playwright). Any change to normalisation or matching edits **both** files and
both tests in the same commit.

## MV3 lifecycle traps already hit

- The service worker is suspended after ~30 s idle; state lives in `chrome.storage`, not in
  module globals. Alarms (`HEALTH_ALARM`, `SWEEP_ALARM`, 1 min) are the only timers.
- Popup showed *no status yet* after suspension → popup now sends `request-status` to the tab on
  open (`background.js`). Keep that pull; do not rely on pushed state alone.
- After *Load unpacked* / reload the content script is **not** injected into an already open
  Discord tab — the tab must be reloaded. Say so whenever you ask the operator to reload.
- Comet Memory Saver must keep `discord.com` active (host setting, done); a discarded tab has no
  observer.

## Trigger contract with Python (`bridge.py`)

`POST /trigger` JSON: `event_id` (`<channel>-<message>`), `channel_id`, `guild_id`,
`message_id`, `matched_target`, `message_ts_ms`, `sent_at_ms`, `detected_at_offset_ms`; shared
secret in the `Authorization` header (paired via `ocarina pair`). Python validates every field
(regexes, ranges, max age), dedupes by `event_id`, checks `matched_target` and the `Origin`
header (`allowed_extension_origin` in `config.toml`). Do not add fields that carry message text or
links; the trigger cannot arm, disarm, reset or alter policy (hard rule 3).

Tests: `tests/test_extension_content.py`, `tests/test_extension_background.py`,
`tests/test_bridge.py`; fixture `tests/fixtures/discord/channel.html` mirrors the live list.
